## 1. Narrow successor purpose

R4 is a successor only for the verified scanner module lifecycle defect
observed during the one permitted R3 actual attempt. It preserves R1–R3 bytes,
the protected-source inventory, seven allowed tuple identities, the closed
24-command inventory, signal behavior, fixture rules and all Host boundaries.

The R4 loader must register the exact hash-verified scanner module before
executing it, then remove that exact module mapping whether loading succeeds or
fails. A collision, a module identity substitution, an unexpected scanner
shape, or any residue is fail-closed.

